From dab72e861ada0ea732bdf4b54e746eea9bd00483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:59:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(output): add per-output render_scale for HiDPI
 supersampling
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Clients are asked to render at render_scale (wp_fractional_scale_v1 and
preferred_buffer_scale) while the scene samples the larger buffers down to
the logical scale raster — the measured-good macOS-style path from #478.
Logical geometry, wl_output.scale, and client UI sizing are untouched;
unset render_scale follows the scale bit-identically. Values below the
logical scale are honored but warned at parse.

X11 joins desktop-wide: xwayland_native_resolution publishes each output
at its render scale through a provider XwaylandOutputs resolves from the
output binding. Direct scanout declines while render_scale != scale
(documented with the buffer-cost trade-off).

The hint has two owners: notifySurfaceScaleIter and the scene layer, which
re-derived max(output scale) on every surface-output change and clobbered
the hint (wire-proven). A scene preferred_scale_provider hook makes the
compositor the single derivation owner; the fields live in wlr_scene's
WLR_PRIVATE tail so the wlroots ABI offsets hold (scene-abi). Dropping the
key on reload must re-notify clients: sameOutputState now compares
renderScale (mutation-probed pin).

Red-first: protocol/render_scale fails on the base tree (client at
150/120, buffer 500x375) and passes after (240/120, 800x600; hot-reload
falls back). Units 142/142; full harness 389 pass / 5 known
environmental failures; remark, clang-format, and clang-tidy clean.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
